# Everything a deployment produces. The repository root already ignores `secrets/` and `keys/` at
# any depth and `*.seed` everywhere, so key material is excluded by construction rather than by this
# file remembering to; these are the runtime artefacts that are specific to `deploy/`.

/var/
/genesis/
/config/kernel-config.json
/config/stozher-gateway.toml
/.env
/backups/
# What `bin/stozher-restore` renames on its two paths: `.superseded-` is the state it moved out of
# the way, `.rejected-` is the archive material it rolled back after the chain failed to verify.
# Both can be a copy of `secrets/` or of `.env`, so both are key material under a name the root
# `.gitignore`'s `secrets/` and `*.seed` rules do not match.
*.superseded-*
*.rejected-*
